  1	# Production deployment
  2	
  3	This repository deploys the Skillplane app and MCP Cloudflare Workers backed by
  4	one PostgreSQL database through Hyperdrive and one private R2 bucket. The
  5	landing Worker is maintained and deployed independently from the 21n monorepo's
  6	`landing/skillplane` workspace. The production hosts are
  7	`skillplane.dev`, `app.skillplane.dev`, and `mcp.skillplane.dev`.
  8	
  9	## One-time provider preparation
 10	
 11	Before the first release:
 12	
 13	1. Create a password-authenticated production PostgreSQL database reachable over
 14	   TLS, enable the provider's managed backup and point-in-time recovery policy,
 15	   and retain its direct URL for migration and backup processes only.
 16	2. Create a Cloudflare Hyperdrive configuration whose origin is that PostgreSQL
 17	   database. Record its 32-character ID. Do not put the direct database URL into
 18	   a Worker variable.
 19	3. Create a production Turnstile widget restricted to
 20	   `app.skillplane.dev`. Record its site key and secret key.
 21	4. Complete Cloudflare Email Service onboarding for `skillplane.dev`, including
 22	   the sender `no-reply@auth.skillplane.dev`, and confirm arbitrary-recipient
 23	   transactional sending is enabled.
 24	5. Confirm the Wrangler identity has Workers Scripts, Workers Routes,
 25	   Hyperdrive read, R2 read/write, and Email Sending permissions. The zone must
 26	   be active in the same Cloudflare account.
