  1	# Nucleus Account Service
  2	
  3	## Environments
  4	
  5	Account API domains are product-owned so browser and WKWebView cookies stay
  6	first-party for each app. The same regional Worker deployment is routed from
  7	each product account hostname.
  8	
  9	| Environment | Domain pattern |
 10	| --- | --- |
 11	| local | `https://account-{region}-local.<product-domain>` |
 12	| dev | `https://account-{region}-dev.<product-domain>` |
 13	| pre | `https://account-{region}-pre.<product-domain>` |
 14	| live | `https://account-{region}.<product-domain>` |
 15	
 16	Current product domains:
 17	
 18	- `nucleum.app`
 19	- `memotron.app`
 20	- `pointron.app`
 21	
 22	Regions:
 23	
 24	- `insouth` placed near `aws:ap-south-1`
 25	- `useast` placed near `aws:us-east-1`
 26	- `euwest` placed near `aws:eu-west-2`
 27	
 28	## Sync Database
 29	
 30	The account service hosts DataFn under `/datafn/*`, but sync data must
 31	use a separate regional database from the AuthFn account database.
 32	
 33	Node entrypoints require:
 34	
 35	```bash
 36	DATAFN_DATABASE_URL=REDACTED
 37	```
 38	
 39	Cloudflare Workers require either a `SYNC_DB` Hyperdrive binding or a
 40	`DATAFN_DATABASE_URL` secret. Do not point these at `DATABASE_URL` or
 41	`ACCOUNT_DB`; AuthFn tables and sync tables are intentionally separate.
 42	
 43	Optional sync settings:
 44	
 45	```bash
 46	DATAFN_DB_POOL_SIZE=5
 47	DATAFN_MAX_PAYLOAD_BYTES=5242880
 48	```
202	If auth behavior looks stale while switching between these modes, clear browser
203	storage/cookies for `nucleum.app`, `memotron.app`, or `pointron.app`, especially
204	the AuthFn session cookies and `authfn:user-region-map`/Nucleus region cache.
205	
206	## Cloudflare Config Source Of Truth
207	
208	`services/account/config/environments.json` is the source of truth for
209	regional account-service infrastructure config:
210	
211	- account/product domains
212	- local/dev/pre/live URL shape
213	- regional Worker env names
214	- Hyperdrive IDs
215	- KV namespace IDs
216	- Durable Object lookup Worker names
217	- placement hints
218	- CORS/OAuth return origins
